+
+# My Math
+
+> The opening page of My Math — Alan's book of the mathematics he hunts down for himself. It carries the standard he dropped on 2026-08-11 and what replaced it: the finding happens where he does the deriving, saying it in his own words in the session is sufficient, and a recorder writes it down behind him. Net markdown bytes added under this book feed the Mathematics value and Lalita's writing economy.
+
+This is where I write down the mathematics I hunt down myself.
+
+I used to say that a result didn't come in here until I could say it in my own
+words, the writing being the proof that I did the finding. That line is gone.
+Saying it in my own words in the session is sufficient — the finding happens
+where I do the deriving, and a recorder writes it down behind me.
